    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0715" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/668</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-12">July 12, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During his call this morning the Chinese Minister asked whether the Government
                    had reached any decision with respect to sending a <pb facs="0716" n="604"
                        xml:id="pg604"/> financial attaché to China. He expressed earnestly his hope
                    that we would find it possible to do so.</p>
                <p>I explained to the Minister that the matter was still undecided and was a subject
                    which was, even now, being discussed with the Treasury Department. I said I
                    hoped we would reach a decision shortly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
